attorneys.bio:
Matt Duffy is a shareholder at Monroe Moxness Berg PA in Minneapolis. Matt divides his legal practice among land use and zoning, business litigation, and real estate matters. He focuses on finding common-sense answers to his clients’ disputes and helps them reach their business objectives through the strategic use of both litigation and non-litigation methods. Matt assists clients with transactional and litigation matters, representing his clients in negotiations, dispute resolution, mediation and arbitration, court hearings, trials, council and board meetings, and at the Minnesota appellate courts.

Matt works with real estate developers, business owners, sand and aggregate producers, and landowners on a wide ranges of issues, including:

Environmental review and due diligence for real estate developments, land acquisitions, site repurposing, leasing and non-metallic aggregate mining and processing facilities;

Commercial real estate disputes and eviction/detainer notices;

Arbitration and mediation of franchisor/franchisee, commercial contracts, construction defects, and warranty disputes;

Landlord/tenant litigation;

Land use planning, including zoning and permitting;

Real estate and boundary matters; and

Commercial, business and general civil disputes.

